  "id": "COMPOUND:766 - PROTEIN:6297",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between estradiol and Ribosomal protein S6 kinase 2 (RPS6K2) through two distinct pathways. In Path 1, estradiol is linked to Sulfotransferase family cytosolic 2B member 1, which in turn is targeted by P-Nitrophenol, and P-Nitrophenol targets RPS6K2. In Path 2, estradiol is directly linked to Monoclonal antibody 2E2, which is targeted by 4-(2-Hydroxyethyl)-5-methyloxazole, and this latter compound targets RPS6K2. Both pathways involve compounds that interact with RPS6K2, suggesting a possible mechanism by which estradiol may influence RPS6K2 activity. The integration of these pathways implies that estradiol could modulate RPS6K2 through either direct or indirect interactions, potentially via the compounds mentioned. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between estradiol and RPS6K2, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
